ARES-6 benchmark ports: third-party licences and provenance
===========================================================

These notices cover the retained third-party material in ares6-air,
ares6-basic, ares6-babylon and ares6-ml. Original notices also remain in the
ported source files and recorded inputs. The code has been transcribed into
strict TypeScript; file headers describe adaptations. These notices do not
replace or expand the permissions granted by the original licensors.

The ARES-6 snapshot is WebKit/WebKit revision:
b64265f153b3178bfb4ca9f51736289f57982fce
https://github.com/WebKit/WebKit/tree/b64265f153b3178bfb4ca9f51736289f57982fce/PerformanceTests/ARES-6

Additional pinned sources are listed with the affected components. The final
section identifies omitted material; its code and licence texts are not
included in these ports.


1. Air and Basic: Apple BSD-2-Clause notice
===========================================

Applies to the Air allocator/support code and benchmark adapter, and to
Basic's interpreter and embedded benchmark programs. Air/README.md supplies
the Air.js project licence. The retained recordings trace to Air.js itself,
Mozilla's Gaussian code and Microsoft's TypeScript scanner; the additional
Gaussian and TypeScript source notices are reproduced in sections 7 and 8.

