13. Provenance exclusions
========================

The following material is deliberately absent. No replacement algorithm is
supplied for an excluded routine.

Air GBEmu recording
-------------------
Air/payload-gbemu-executeIteration.js records code from Octane/GBEmu. The
identified Octane source explicitly carries GPL-2.0, so the recording is
excluded. Air therefore retains three of the four original recorded inputs.

Evidence:
https://github.com/WebKit/WebKit/blob/b64265f153b3178bfb4ca9f51736289f57982fce/PerformanceTests/ARES-6/Air/payload-gbemu-executeIteration.js
https://github.com/chromium/octane/blob/570ad1ccfe86e3eecba0636c8f932ac08edec517/gbemu-part1.js

ML decompositions and dependent APIs
-----------------------------------
The bundled LU, SVD, Cholesky, eigenvalue and QR routines explicitly identify
Mapack as a source. Preserved original Mapack history at the revision below
provides only a warranty disclaimer, without a redistribution grant under
one of the permitted licences. These sections are excluded as unclear in
provenance. This is not a claim that Mapack is GPL-licensed.

The SVD supplemental threshold/solve/inverse section also links to and
closely follows Accord.NET source carrying LGPL-2.1-or-later. The overall
ml.js MIT notice is not treated as permission to include those sections.

The five decompositions, their decomposition utilities, dependent inverse,
solve, determinant and pseudoinverse APIs, and associated aliases are omitted.
The original neural-network benchmark does not call these routines.

